  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Midnight Atlas",
    "overview": "Atlas places a luminous green map illustration between a compact midnight tool bar and a sculpted comparison dock. Electric blue marks the selected candidate; icy cyan carries Directions. The user selected the original Atlas reference (`.impeccable/mocks/atlas-approved.png`) and explicitly requested its supplied map illustration and reference values. This replaces the City Edition visual record with the implemented Atlas system.\n\nThe default screen is the functional Atlas scientific explorer, implemented by `src/App.tsx`, `src/atlas.css` and `src/components/ActivityMap.tsx`; `?view=scientific` remains compatible. The fixed reference illustration is available explicitly at `?view=illustration`, implemented in `src/IllustratedAtlas.tsx` and `src/illustrated-atlas.css`. Its supplied raster asset is `src/assets/atlas-illustration.png`; origin and drawn markers are embedded artwork. Phone destination selection opens its actionable detail sheet. Narrow short screens keep two-column toolbar controls; the four-column short layout is restricted to widths of at least560px. Touch inputs use16px type to avoid focus zoom. PROJECT.md remains canonical product authority. These are distinct visual/data surfaces. This document records implementation, not scientific validation or an automated fidelity pass.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Midnight framing, dimensional blue selection and cyan actions.",
      "A supplied illustrated map cropped with CSS rather than redrawn geography.",
      "Native text, controls, candidate selection and modal disclosures around the image.",
      "A horizontal desktop comparison dock that becomes stacked rows on phones.",
      "An explicit path from fixed reference content to the preserved scientific explorer."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
